<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar production tops 4.0 million tonnes.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar production tops 4.0 million tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's sugar production reached 4.21 million tonnes as of March 4 compared with 4.19 million tonnes in the corresponding period last year, industry sources said.</p>
<p>Although the amount surpassed that of the previous season, the rise was caused mostly by increased capacity but the yield still trailed that posted in 1995/96.</p>
<p>As of March 4, a total of 41.74 million tonnes of sugar cane was crushed to produce 2.48 million tonnes of raw sugar and 1.73 million tonnes of white sugar.</p>
<p>But the yield was recorded at 100.98 kg of sugar per tonne of sugar cane versus 104.40 kg last season.</p>
<p>The following is the comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period in the last season (in tonnes unless otherwise specified):</p>
<p>				 March 4, 1997	March 4, 1996</p>
<p>Crushed sugar cane	    41,743,460	   40,097,052</p>
<p>Raw sugar			  2,483,372	    2,441,581</p>
<p>White and refined sugar	1,731,850	    1,744,610</p>
<p>Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	11.44		  11.97</p>
<p>Yield				   100.98		 104.40</p>
<p>Molasses			   1,759,218	    1,828,393</p>
<p>Yield				    42.14		   45.60</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
